    "created_at": "2022-06-08T06:49:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-06-08T06:49:10Z",
    "body": "This suggestion as well as \"true latin1\" (or isomorphic decode/encode as per Infra) have come up from time-to-time. Thus far we haven't acted on them as they:\r\n\r\n* lack good use cases;\r\n* can be written in JavaScript directly without much hassle; and\r\n* they are not a part of the web platform's current text encoding infrastructure and we don't want to expand that as new things ought to use UTF-8 exclusively.",
